  - mark_dlq_permanent: Flag a DLQ entry as `human_required` — pulls it out of future `replay_dlq_by_category` scans and writes the operator's reason to the audit trail. Use when analysis shows a persistent bug that auto-replay would just re-hit. Doesn't change job.status — the entry stays in DLQ, just won't be auto-replayed. Idempotent.
    input_schema={"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"job_id": {"format": "uuid", "title": "Job Id", "type": "string"}, "reason": {"description": "Full sentence explaining why the entry is not replayable. Written to the audit log for the human review path.", "maxLength": 1024, "minLength": 8, "title": "Reason", "type": "string"}, "idempotency_key": {"maxLength": 255, "minLength": 8, "title": "Idempotency Key", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["job_id", "reason", "idempotency_key"], "title": "MarkDlqPermanentInput", "type": "object"}
  - pause_dag: Pause promotion of WAITING children in the DAG rooted at `root_job_id`. Observable effect: `get_dag_state(root_job_id)` returns `paused=true` with `paused_expires_in_seconds`, children stay in status `waiting`, and no new promotions occur while the flag is set. Already-RUNNING jobs are not cancelled — pause stops promotion, it does not stop work in flight. Self-cleans on TTL (default 10 minutes), after which held children promote automatically. Idempotent.
